# {{ COMPANY_NAME }} — People

Inherits from `../../company/CLAUDE.md`. This file adds dept-specific scope.

## Mission

Owns capability gap → resource allocation. AI-first: every gap is first evaluated for AI-agent suitability via [`allocate-resource`](../../.claude/skills/allocate-resource/); human hire is the fallback only for tasks requiring lived human experience, physical-world action, or legally-mandated human accountability. People does NOT manage the org chart's authority structure — that's `ceo`'s domain; people surfaces evidence and proposed routes.

## Roles

- `people-lead` — dept lead, runs `allocate-resource` for every capability gap; maintains the resource registry of all agents + humans. Defined at [`.claude/agents/people/people-lead.md`](../../.claude/agents/people/people-lead.md).

(Sub-roles can be added later via [`design-agent`](../../.claude/skills/design-agent/) when the dept load justifies splitting.)

## Escalation

`people-lead` → `ceo` (for org-chart changes + hiring budget approval). Internal AI route delegates to `ops-manager` for `design-agent` invocation.

## Data scopes

- `data/` (dept-internal): the resource registry (CSV/markdown index of all agents + humans + their capabilities), AI-first decision-tree audit logs.
- `../../company/hiring/`: human-route job specs (see [`company/hiring/README.md`](../../company/hiring/README.md) for the lifecycle).

## Processes-as-skills convention

Dept-scoped skills live at `.claude/skills/<name>/` (nested within this dept folder). Cross-dept skills live at the repo root `.claude/skills/`. `allocate-resource` (the AI-first kernel) lives at the ROOT `.claude/skills/` because it's invoked by/for every dept.

